<p>The 315 fps IBO rating applies at the top of the range: a 30" draw and 70 lb. A youth archer shooting 25 lb at a 24" draw will see far lower arrow speeds, which is exactly what you want while they learn.</p>

<h2 id="h-who-the-legit-maxx-is-for">Who Should Buy the Bear Legit Maxx?</h2>
<p>The Bear Legit Maxx makes the most sense for shooters whose draw length or strength is still changing:</p>
<ul class="checks">
  <li><strong>Kids and teens</strong> who will grow several inches over the next few seasons.</li>
  <li><strong>Adult beginners</strong> who want to start light and build strength without buying a second bow.</li>
  <li><strong>Families</strong> who want one bow that can be re-set for different shooters (with a pro shop&rsquo;s help).</li>
  <li><strong>Hunters returning after an injury</strong> who need to rebuild draw weight gradually.</li>
</ul>
<p>If you are an adult with a settled draw length and you already pull 60 lb or more comfortably, a dedicated adult hunting bow will usually give you more speed and refinement for the money.</p>

